{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact notes-only head 70dee51e3dbfe859c382b975bdfba93e9c80c6e1 on builder/up1-upgrade-act-20261117, its 1 artifact, for request b12f2613 under my promise c454c597. The implementation is UP-1 (request d7f77eeb, promise 906f29fc). The reporting artifact is `notes/2026-11-17-application-upgrade.md`, status proposed. The head's parent is main b2477fd3.\n\nWhat I read: the whole note against the five request conditions.\n\n1. A proposed note under `notes/` for the replace form, for Hugh's decision: met.\n2. Scene first: met. Ana upgrades Counter 0.6.0 to 0.7.0, with what she runs, what members see and what happens to the old scope, the screen and the archive.\n3. What it touches, with file:line, and the cost for a room with two superseded items: met. Section 2 covers the item, the rules definition, the reader, the screen route, the archive proof and the wake record. Section 3 gives the cost table.\n4. Options and one recommendation, with Hugh's kernel decisions named: met. A (present in place), B (replace) and C (replace and close). It recommends A and B as one act chosen by the semantic identifier, and names two kernel and two room decisions.\n5. Notes only: met. The head changes one file under `notes/`.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Citations. I read eight of them at the head, and seven match: the reader's `active` check (`application-install-reader.ts:32`), the route comment on a stable hostname (`route.ts:23-25`), `Status` (`read.ts:49`), the identity comparison (`archive-packages.ts:130-131`), the pending-or-stop split (`archive-packages.ts:111-112`), the proof's `pending` and unsupported refusals (`archive-proof.ts:73-74`) and the MCP card drop on two active installations (`service.ts:353-356`). The item's states sit on `application-install.ts:32`, not line 31 as section 2.1 says.\n- Counter 0.7.0 is a presentation change. `apps/counter/release-identifiers.json` keeps semantic `a5a44ebc` and entry `b5582434` and moves only the presentation to `9d6995c8`, as the scene says.\n- The cost table is consistent with the AR-1 and AR-4 rates. Its central point holds: an in-place upgrade without the archive change in section 2.5 starts the hourly retry loop, about 340 to 670 requests a day for each scope, and step U2 owes a red for it.\n- The gate. END 41c75379 passed. The head is notes-only, so the gate skipped its test step. The last lines of `gate.txt` read \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\".\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean.\n\nArchitecture: sound for a proposal. Choosing the form from the semantic identifier keeps one act for both cases. It also matches the existing route comment, which already expects a presentation update to keep its hostname.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding for a notes-only head. One point for Hugh's decision, and for U1 if he agrees: option A names `semantic` and `definition` as the values that must not change. It should also hold `publisher` fixed, and it should require the new release to be one that `APPLICATION_TRUST` names. Otherwise an in-place upgrade could move an item to a release from another publisher. Section 2.1 lists `publisher` among the item's fixed values, so the note only needs to say it.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The line number in section 2.1 can move to 32 in a later edit.\n\nThis approval decides nothing for Hugh and authorizes no push or landing. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a0105afbf19dfffe51d7ab3a31d16881fb257b4c","binding":"assigned","head":"70dee51e3dbfe859c382b975bdfba93e9c80c6e1","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c454c59796ebe4a7e40494f71414822e3d6154b2\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:906f29fc5f644bbdb1cf37d4ab01ecbbe0443757\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1